(Tenxo is a decentralized GPU compute marketplace with four main planes:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Frontend: Next.js app for providers, consumers, marketplace, billing, and account workflows.) Tj
T*
(- Matchmaker API: Go HTTP service that owns auth, job state, node state, billing integration,) Tj
T*
(  storage presign, and WebSocket job updates.) Tj
T*
(- Orchestration bus: NATS JetStream work queue for job dispatch plus NATS subjects for node) Tj
T*
(  heartbeat and job result events.) Tj
T*
(- Workers and clients: Rust edge agent advertises GPUs and executes jobs; Python CLI/client) Tj
T*
(  packages and the web app submit encrypted workloads.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(PostgreSQL is the source of truth for nodes, jobs, API keys, usage records, billing customers,) Tj
T*
(and payment transaction history. Object storage is Cloudflare R2 in production, with local) Tj
T*
(encrypted upload storage for development.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Services) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `frontend`: Next.js 14 UI. Uses Supabase auth, matchmaker REST APIs, and `/ws` for live job) Tj
T*
(  lifecycle updates.) Tj
T*
(- `backend`: Go matchmaker. Validates Supabase JWTs or Tenxo API keys, lists inventory,) Tj
T*
(  creates jobs, signs storage URLs, stores usage, and proxies Razorpay billing operations.) Tj
T*
(- `edge_agent`: Rust worker. Publishes heartbeats, reports GPU metadata and TEE status,) Tj
T*
(  consumes work, uploads encrypted results.) Tj
T*
(- `tenxo`: Python package and CLI. Packs/encrypts workloads, calls presign/job APIs, and) Tj
T*
(  downloads encrypted results.) Tj
T*
(- `nats`: JetStream broker. `jobs` stream uses work-queue retention for worker consumption;) Tj
T*
(  `jobs.results` reports completion.) Tj
T*
(- `postgres`: Persistent metadata and billing state.) Tj
T*
(- `r2/object storage`: Encrypted job payload and result blobs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
